{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<div
  id="{{ section.id }}"
  class="section-{{ section.id }}-padding"
  style="background-color: {{ section.settings.background_color }}">
  <div class="page-width">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 md:gap-8">
      {% for block in section.blocks %}
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <img
            class="size-7 md:size-10"
            src="{{ block.settings.perk_image | image_url: width: 150 }}"
            loading="lazy"
            height="{{ block.settings.perk_image.height }}"
            width="{{ block.settings.perk_image.width }}"
            alt="Perk Image">
          <h3 class="text-base md:text-lg my-0 text-center font-semibold text-black">{{ block.settings.perk_title }}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm md:text-base my-0 text-center text-slate-700">{{ block.settings.perk_content }}</p>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  FUEL_06: the Search & Compare fragrance finder rides inside this section
  because templates/index.json sits at Shopify's 25 section cap and a new
  homepage section is impossible without removing client content. The design
  puts the band immediately after this benefits row and before the Trustpilot
  block, which is exactly here. Same approach as the FUEL_05 home row.

  Homepage only. This section file is also used by thirteen product templates
  and the finder must not appear on any of them: request.page_type carries the
  gate, and the homepage section id is the belt to those braces, because the
  editor bot rewrites templates/index.json from editor state several times a
  day and a section deleted and re-added in the editor comes back under a new
  id. Either test alone keeps the band alive on the homepage, and neither can
  ever put it on a product page.

  It ships hidden. Nothing below is visible until Intelligems puts
  ab-f06-finder on the html element, so with the test off the homepage renders
  exactly as it does today.

  No new block type is added to this section: the loop above renders every
  block as a perk with no case guard, so a FUEL_06 block would draw a broken
  perk tile alongside the finder. The copy lives in section settings instead,
  which also means the Swedish translation is a theme editor edit rather than
  a deploy.

  Remove this block with the FUEL_06 cleanup.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if request.page_type == 'index' or section.id contains 'feature_highlights_wfUacV' -%}
  {% render 'fuel06-finder', section: section, mode: 'assets' %}
  {% render 'fuel06-finder', section: section, mode: 'home' %}
{%- elsif request.page_type == 'product' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Product page (2026-09-30): the dialog alone, opened by the link that
    snippets/reactive-variant-selector.liquid renders under the buy button. This section sits
    on every perfume template, so the dialog and its copy travel with it; a
    template without it has no dialog and the link stays hidden.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% render 'fuel06-finder', section: section, mode: 'assets' %}
  {% render 'fuel06-finder', section: section, mode: 'dialog' %}
{%- endif -%}

